# WOFF2 / folderOpen dropper (mandatory clone gate)

A JS trojan was shipped as a fake font and auto-run via VS Code/Cursor tasks. Treat **every GitHub clone** as infected until this scan is clean.

## Clone process (strict)

1. `git clone` into a folder. Do **not** open that folder as a trusted Cursor/VS Code workspace yet (`folderOpen` is the launcher).
2. Do **not** run `node` on any `*.woff2`. Do **not** `npm install` / `pub get` / `pod install` until the scan is clean.
3. Run the scan below in the clone root (read-only: `file`, `head`, `grep`, `python3` to inspect bytes). Never execute the hits.
4. If any IOC hits: stop, report paths, wait. Do not “fix” by running attacker scripts.
5. Only after a clean scan: open the folder in Cursor and install packages.

## Nature of the dropper (what it looks like)

Identical kit was copied into unrelated apps (Flutter, Nest, HTML, meta-repos).

### 1. `public/fonts/fa-solid-400.woff2` — fake font, real JavaScript

- Labeled as Font Awesome; `file` says **ASCII text**, not `wOF2`.
- Leading whitespace padding, then Node: `global.i="A10-*010"` or `global.i = 'A11--#'`, `require("http")` / `https` / `zlib` / `child_process.spawn`, `eval`.
- Size seen: ~8943 bytes (A10-*010), ~27414 (A11), **32874 (A10-*020)**, ~32645 (re-infect).
- **Never** `node public/fonts/fa-solid-400.woff2`.

### 2. Camouflage Font Awesome kit — `public/fonts/`

Real font bytes used as cover. Same hashes across infected repos. **Not used** by the apps. Fake README claims “Blockchain Explorer” / `public/index.html`.

Typical names (all of these belong to the kit):

- `public/fonts/README.md` (Blockchain Explorer lie)
- `fa-brands-400.{eot,svg,ttf,woff,woff2}`
- `fa-regular-400.{eot,svg,ttf,woff,woff2}`
- `fa-solid-900.{eot,svg,ttf,woff,woff2}`

Do **not** confuse with real app fonts (e.g. DFC frontend **Manrope** `.otf`). Leave those.

### 3. `.vscode/tasks.json` — hidden auto-run

- `label`: `eslint-check`, `"hide": true`, `"runOn": "folderOpen"`
- Command: `node ./public/fonts/fa-solid-400.woff2` (unix + Windows `where node` fallback)
- Fires when the folder is opened as a trusted workspace.

### 4. `.vscode/settings.json` — enables auto tasks

- `"task.allowAutomaticTasks": true`
- Nested `"tasks"` with `"runOn": "folderOpen"` and decoy `npm run lint`
- SST / Windows / `jest.unit.config.cjs` / `compile-hero` noise in apps that are not SST

### 5. Other identical planted JSON

- `.vscode/launch.json` — copy-pasted SST debug (`Debug SST`, `AWS_PROFILE`: `flo-ct-flo360`)
- `.vscode/extensions.json` — plantuml + prettier recommendations
- `.vscode/spellright.dict` — `Contentful` / `Lerna`

If these four `.vscode` files are **byte-identical** across unrelated repos, they are the kit. Delete the kit; do not keep “maybe useful” settings.

### 6. Config tails (build-time — font 404 is not clean)

Same family. Files **anywhere** in the tree: `postcss.config.js`, `postcss.config.mjs`, `babel.config.js`, `tailwind.config.js`, `tailwind.config.cjs`.

- Real: tens–~1400 B, no `global.i=`
- Kit: ~33 KB, `global.i="A10-*1909-10"`
- Nested misses: `front-end/postcss.config.mjs`, `web/postcss.config.mjs`

Keep Cursor user setting `"task.allowAutomaticTasks": "off"`.

## Scan commands (clone root)

```bash
# fake JS font
find . -name 'fa-solid-400.woff2' -not -path '*/.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*'
# camouflage kit
find . -path '*/public/fonts/fa-*' -not -path '*/.git/*'
# launcher
find . -path '*/.vscode/tasks.json' -not -path '*/.git/*'
grep -R -n -E 'folderOpen|allowAutomaticTasks|fa-solid-400\.woff2|eslint-check|A10-\*010|A10-\*020|A10-\*1909-10|A11--#' \
  --include='*.json' --include='*.woff2' --include='README.md' --include='*.js' --include='*.mjs' --include='*.cjs' \
  --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=node_modules .

# config tails (any directory)
find . \( -name 'postcss.config.js' -o -name 'postcss.config.mjs' -o -name 'babel.config.js' \
  -o -name 'tailwind.config.js' -o -name 'tailwind.config.cjs' \) \
  -not -path '*/.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -print0 \
  | xargs -0 -I{} sh -c 'wc -c "$1"; grep -l "global.i=" "$1" 2>/dev/null' _ {}
```

Classify a `.woff2` with `file` + first bytes: magic `wOF2` = font; ASCII/`require(`/`eval` after whitespace = malware.

## If GitHub still has the kit

Local clean checkouts can be re-infected by `git pull` / fresh clone from an unpurged remote. `pickle-ball-app` went 404 on 28 Aug and was dirty again before the 8 Sep wash. Do not fetch infected refs into a clean tree. After a remote wash, **re-clone** — do not pull an old mixed tree. Living notes: `vibe-coding/docs/POLINRIDER-WASH-2026-09-08.md`.
